| `input_adb_lookup(a.csv)`
```### Map source lookup to source name ###```
| eval source=case(source_lookup="a.csv", "a")
```### Keep only the columns the merge uses ###```
| fields _time, source, source_lookup, os, owner, empty
```### Split multivalue fields ###```
| foreach os, owner, empty [eval <<FIELD>>=split(<<FIELD>>, "|")]
```### Ignore values ###```
| eval os = mvfilter(NOT (in(os, "null", "none", "unknown"))), owner = mvfilter(NOT (in(owner, "say \"hi\"", "<b>&", "it's")))
| search _key=*
```### Tag multivalue values with their time (so the most recent ones can be kept) ###```
| eval `adb_tag_time(os)`, `adb_tag_time(owner)`, `adb_tag_time(empty)`
| stats values(source) as source, values(source_lookup) as source_lookup, max(_time) as last_seen, values(os) as os, values(owner) as owner, values(empty) as empty by _key
```### Merge: only the keys go through adbmerge, the result is joined back by row id ###```
| `adb_merge(25, 50)`
```### Clusters that were too large to merge go to assetdb_overflow for review, not into assetdb ###```
| `adb_save_overflow`
| where isnull(adb_overflow)
| eval _key = md5(mvjoin(mvsort(asset), "::"))
| stats values(asset) as asset, values(source) as source, values(source_lookup) as source_lookup, max(last_seen) as last_seen, `adb_counters`, values(os) as os, values(owner) as owner, values(empty) as empty by _key
```### Newest values first: sort, de-duplicate and strip the time prefix ###```
| eval `adb_newest_first(os)`, `adb_newest_first(owner)`, `adb_newest_first(empty)`
```### Trim multivalue fields ###```
| eval os = mvindex(os,0,4), owner = mvindex(owner,0,4), empty = mvindex(empty,0,4)
```### Run safety: how many assets did the last successful run produce? ###```
| `adb_run_guard(0.5)`
```### Record this run in assetdb_runs (the last 200 runs are kept) ###```
| `adb_record_run(0.5, 200)`
```### Only write the asset database when the run passed the safety check ###```
| `adb_write_gate`
```### Output to KV store ###```
| table _key, asset, source, source_lookup, last_seen, os, owner, empty
| outputlookup override_if_empty=false assetdb
